{#
  Case studies, bento grid.

  All the studies at a glance instead of one at a time: a tall lead card beside
  a stack of smaller ones, each one a photograph with the copy sat over it.

  WHAT REVEALS — deliberately little. The card shows one short line from
  `blurb`; hovering slides up one more from `highlight`, set as plain body copy
  rather than as a pull quote. Revealing a whole paragraph was tried and it made
  the cards work too hard for a grid whose job is to be scanned. A study with no
  `highlight` simply does not expand.

  Expects the same `studies` array as case-carousel.njk, plus the same
  `carouselEyebrow` / `carouselTitle` / `carouselLead`.

  A study needs `name` (or `client`) and `blurb` to look right here. The
  hand-written `caseStudy` in a service page's front matter has neither, which
  is why only the private water supplies page uses this layout so far: the other
  three would need a one-line `blurb` writing for their lead study first. Every
  field is guarded, so a missing one leaves nothing out of place rather than an
  empty hole.

  SURFACE — `bentoSurface` picks the section behind the grid: omit it for navy,
  or pass "section--light" / "section--paper". The cards carry .theme-dark and
  so stay dark whatever sits behind them, because the copy is set over a
  photograph and needs the contrast; on a light section they read as dark objects
  on cream rather than a navy band, which is the point of putting them there.

  HOW IT HANDLES THE COUNT — three is the layout the grid is built for: a lead
  card spanning two rows on the left and two stacked on the right. A page that
  owns fewer than three studies BORROWS from the rest of the file to make the
  set up, so the two-up and one-up fallbacks below are now only a safety net for
  a data file with fewer than three studies in it at all:
    2  two equal cards side by side
    1  one wide card
  Anything past three is dropped, same ceiling as the carousel.

  ON A PHONE the card stops being a photograph with text over it. The picture
  sits on top with only the tags and the name over its foot; the body copy sits
  underneath it on the card. Nothing hides behind a hover that cannot happen.

  NEEDS PHOTOGRAPHY. Every card is a picture, so with `image: null` the grid is
  three navy panels. Until real project photos exist this reads worse than the
  editorial layout, not better.
#}
{#
  TOP UP TO THREE. The grid is at its best as three cards, and a service with
  only one or two studies of its own would otherwise drop to a two-up. So the
  short ones borrow from the rest of the file.

  Borrowed studies come LAST, after whatever the page owns, so the page's own
  work still leads and takes the tall card. They are not badged as borrowed:
  the section only ever claims to be selected work, and the tags on each card
  already say which county it is in. Taken in file order unless a page sets
  `bentoTopUp` (an array of study ids) to choose them by hand.

  The slice makes a copy first, so pushing here cannot mutate the array the
  including page built.
#}
{% if studies %}
  {% set studies = studies.slice(0, 3) %}
  {% if studies.length < 3 and caseStudies %}
    {% set used = [] %}
    {% for cs in studies %}{% set _ = used.push(cs.id or cs.name) %}{% endfor %}
    {% for id in bentoTopUp or [] %}
      {% for cs in caseStudies %}
        {% if cs.id == id and studies.length < 3 and cs.id not in used %}{% set _ = studies.push(cs) %}{% set _ = used.push(cs.id) %}{% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% for cs in caseStudies %}
      {% if studies.length < 3 and cs.id not in used %}{% set _ = studies.push(cs) %}{% set _ = used.push(cs.id) %}{% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  {% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if studies and studies.length %}
<section class="section {{ bentoSurface }} case-bento case-bento--{{ studies.length }}" aria-labelledby="bento-title-{{ carouselId or 'x' }}">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-bento__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ carouselEyebrow or "Selected work" }}</p>
      <h2 id="bento-title-{{ carouselId or 'x' }}" class="statement case-bento__title">{{ carouselTitle | safe or "Projects like this, <span class='em'>across the South East.</span>" }}</h2>
      {% if carouselLead %}<p class="case-bento__lead">{{ carouselLead | safe }}</p>{% endif %}
    </div>

    <ul class="bento" role="list">
      {% for cs in studies %}
      {%- set more = cs.highlight -%}
      <li class="bento__cell">
        <article class="bento__card theme-dark">
          <div class="bento__media" aria-hidden="true">
            {% if cs.image %}
            <img src="{{ cs.image }}" alt="" loading="lazy">
            {% else %}
            <div class="bento__ph"><span>Project photo to follow</span></div>
            {% endif %}
          </div>

          <div class="bento__copy">
            <div class="bento__head">
              {% if cs.flagship or cs.county or cs.location %}
              <p class="bento__tags">
                {% if cs.flagship %}<span class="bento__tag">Flagship project</span>{% endif %}
                {% if cs.county or cs.location %}<span class="bento__tag">{{ cs.county or cs.location }}</span>{% endif %}
              </p>
              {% endif %}
              <h3 class="bento__name">{{ cs.name or cs.client }}</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="bento__text">
              {% if cs.blurb %}<p class="bento__blurb">{{ cs.blurb }}</p>{% endif %}
              {% if more %}
              <div class="bento__reveal"><p class="bento__more">{{ more }}</p></div>
              {% endif %}
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>

    {# Page control for the phone/tablet swipe track. carousel.js fills it in;
       with no JS the track is still swipeable and this stays empty. #}
    {% if studies.length > 1 %}
    <div class="bento__dots" role="tablist" aria-label="Case studies"></div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}
